📚 What I Learned Today
Migrations are the version history of your database schema, not just files that create tables.
Services encapsulate business workflows, allowing multiple entry points (API, CLI, admin, background tasks) to reuse the same logic.
Views should coordinate requests and responses, not implement business rules.
Designing the workflow before writing code leads to cleaner, more maintainable software.


📚 What I Learned Today
Validation, orchestration, and enforcement happen at different layers.
Services should return domain objects, while views return HTTP responses.
Database constraints remain the ultimate guarantee of data integrity.
Business rules describe what must happen; implementation details describe how it happens.

